+++ b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+# leanvm-sidecar
+
+A long-lived leanVM prover and verifier for one client process on the same machine. The client and the sidecar share one file on tmpfs: payloads sit in an arena inside it, and two rings of 64-byte messages carry requests and responses. The client can be written in any language that can map a file and do an atomic 64-bit load and store.
+
+It serves four operations, on leanXMSS signatures only:
+
+| op | what it does |
+| --- | --- |
+| `AGGREGATE` | prove a batch of `(pubkey, message, signature)` |
+| `RECURSE` | prove the union of up to 16 proofs' claims |
+| `VERIFY` | check a proof against its claims |
+| `VERIFY_NARROW` | check a proof, then prove a subset of its claims |
+
+[`PROTOCOL.md`](PROTOCOL.md) is the byte-level specification: the file layout, the messages, the payload encodings and the status codes.
+
+## Build and run
+
+Release only: the guest compiler overflows the debug stack.
+
+```bash
+cargo build --release -p leanvm-sidecar
+target/release/leanvm-sidecar --path /dev/shm/leanvm --threads 16
+```
+
+The sidecar builds the guest, runs its warm-up, creates the channel file and prints `serving <path>`. The file appears only once it is ready, so a client may open it as soon as it exists. Stop the sidecar with a signal; it holds no state to flush.
+
+| flag | default | meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `--path` | required | the channel file; put it on tmpfs (`/dev/shm`) |
+| `--threads` | one per physical core | prover threads; verification always runs on one |
+| `--arena-mib` | 64 | arena size; the payload and the response region of every request in flight have to fit |
+| `--ring-cap` | 64 | slots in each ring, a power of two |
+| `--warmup-signatures` | 1500 | signatures in the warm-up proofs; 0 skips the warm-up |
+| `--warmup-rates` | `1,2` | the `log_inv_rate` values to warm up |
+| `--tracing` | off | print a timing tree per request (`RUST_LOG` sets the level) |
+
+The warm-up is the discarded pass the benchmarks run before they measure: for each rate, one aggregation, one verification and one 16-wide recursion over signatures the sidecar makes for itself. Without it the first request of each shape is slower than the rest. Set `--warmup-signatures` to the largest batch expected and `--warmup-rates` to the rates requests will ask for.
+
+The whole file is faulted in at start, so the arena's memory is committed from then on.
+
+Requests are served one at a time, in order. A request in flight when the sidecar stops is lost; requests still queued are served after a restart on the same file. The header's `epoch` changes on every start, which is how a client notices.
+
+## Clients
+
+Each client exposes the same two calls, over raw payload bytes in the encodings of `PROTOCOL.md`:
+
+- `send(op, flags, log_inv_rate, payload, resp_cap)` copies the payload into the arena, reserves `resp_cap` bytes for the response and queues the request. It returns the request's id, or reports that the ring or the arena is full; it never blocks.
+- `try_recv()` (`tryRecv` in Java and TypeScript) returns the next response with its body copied out, or nothing if the sidecar has not produced one.
+
+| language | where | notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Rust | [`crates/leanvm_sidecar_client`](../../crates/leanvm_sidecar_client) | depends on `libc` alone; links nothing of the prover |
+| Go | [`clients/go`](clients/go) | package `leanvmsidecar`, standard library only |
+| Java | [`clients/java`](clients/java) | `leanvmsidecar.Client`, Java 17 or later, no dependencies; channel files under 2 GiB |
+| TypeScript | [`clients/typescript`](clients/typescript) | Node 18 or later; `client.ts` plus a small C addon (`mmap.c`) that maps the file, since Node cannot; `./build.sh` builds both into `dist/` |
+
+A client is for one thread at a time. Open one only while no request of an earlier client is outstanding: the sidecar would write that request's response into arena space the new client hands out again.
+
+The clients build no payloads and parse no bodies. The end-to-end runners below are the worked example in each language: `crates/leanvm_sidecar_client/examples/e2e.rs`, `clients/go/e2e/main.go`, `clients/java/leanvmsidecar/E2e.java` and `clients/typescript/e2e.ts`.
+
+## End-to-end test
+
+```bash
+bins/leanvm-sidecar/e2e.sh <rust|go|java|ts> <threads> [aggregate-log-inv-rate=2] [recurse-log-inv-rate=1]
+```
+
+The script builds the sidecar and the chosen language's runner, starts the sidecar with `<threads>` prover threads, and has the runner make sixteen `AGGREGATE` requests of 1500 signatures each, one after the other, then one `RECURSE` over the sixteen proofs. Each step prints its request, its response and the time from `send` to the response, as the client sees it. The script stops the sidecar and removes the channel file when the runner exits.
+
+```bash
+bins/leanvm-sidecar/e2e.sh go 16        # Go client, 16 threads, default rates
+bins/leanvm-sidecar/e2e.sh java 32 1 2  # Java client, aggregate at rate 1, recurse at rate 2
+```
+
+The signatures are `testdata/signatures-24000.bin`: 24000 records of `pubkey | message | signature`, every record a different signer, signer `i` on message `i mod 4`. The signers are mock keys, real only at the leaf index they sign at; their signatures verify like any other. If the file is missing the script regenerates it with `examples/gen_signatures.rs`, which takes a minute or two.
+
+The Go runner needs `go` on `PATH`. The Java runner uses `javac` and `java` if they are on `PATH`, and otherwise the `eclipse-temurin:21-jdk` image through `docker`. The TypeScript runner needs `node`, `npm` and a C compiler: the script runs `clients/typescript/build.sh`, which installs the TypeScript compiler from npm on first use.
+
+## Tests
+
+```bash
+cargo test --release -p leanvm-sidecar -p leanvm_sidecar_client
+(cd bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go && go test ./...)
+(cd bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/typescript && ./build.sh && npm test)
+```
+
+The sidecar's test runs every op, and its failure cases, through the Rust client against the serving loop in one process.
diff --git a/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/client.go b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/client.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..5d4c82fe1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/client.go
@@ -0,0 +1,243 @@
+// Package leanvmsidecar is a client of the leanvm-sidecar service: Send a request, TryRecv its response.
+//
+// Payloads and response bodies are raw bytes in the encodings of PROTOCOL.md. It mirrors the Rust
+// client in crates/leanvm_sidecar_client.
+//
+// One Client per channel, used from one goroutine at a time. Open it while no request of an earlier
+// client is outstanding: the server would write that request's response into arena space this
+// client hands out again.
+//
+// Little-endian hosts only: the ring counters are read as native words.
+package leanvmsidecar
+
+import (
+	"encoding/binary"
+	"errors"
+	"os"
+	"sync/atomic"
+	"syscall"
+	"unsafe"
+)
+
+const (
+	OpAggregate    uint32 = 1
+	OpRecurse      uint32 = 2
+	OpVerify       uint32 = 3
+	OpVerifyNarrow uint32 = 4
+
+	// FlagVerifyChildren makes OpRecurse verify every child natively before proving.
+	FlagVerifyChildren uint32 = 1
+
+	StOK                uint32 = 0
+	StBadRequest        uint32 = 1
+	StRespTooSmall      uint32 = 2
+	StInvalidProof      uint32 = 3
+	StAggregationFailed uint32 = 4
+)
+
+const (
+	magic   = 0x48534d564e41454c // "LEANVMSH"
+	version = 1
+	msgSize = 64
+
+	hMagic      = 0
+	hVersion    = 8
+	hEpoch      = 16
+	hRingCap    = 24
+	hTotal      = 32
+	hReqRing    = 40
+	hRespRing   = 48
+	hArenaOff   = 56
+	hArenaLen   = 64
+	hPubKeySize = 72
+	hMessageLen = 80
+	hSigSize    = 88
+	headerSize  = 96
+
+	rHead  = 0
+	rTail  = 64
+	rSlots = 128
+)
+
+// ErrFull: the request ring or the arena has no room. Receive a response and retry.
+var ErrFull = errors.New("leanvmsidecar: no room in the request ring or the arena")
+
+var errHeader = errors.New("leanvmsidecar: not a leanvm-sidecar channel of this version")
+
+type Response struct {
+	// ID is what Send returned for the request.
+	ID     uint64
+	Status uint32
+	Detail uint32
+	// RespLen is the body's length, or under StRespTooSmall the response capacity the request needed.
+	RespLen uint64
+	// Body is the op's response under StOK, UTF-8 text for a human on a failure, empty under StRespTooSmall.
+	Body []byte
+}
+
+// block is a request's arena region: its payload, then its response region. Offsets from the arena's start.
+type block struct {
+	id         uint64
+	off        uint64
+	payloadLen uint64
+	respCap    uint64
+}
+
+func (b block) end() uint64 { return b.off + b.payloadLen + b.respCap }
+
+type Client struct {
+	data     []byte
+	ringCap  uint64
+	reqRing  uint64
+	respRing uint64
+	arenaOff uint64
+	arenaLen uint64
+	nextID   uint64
+	// Blocks of requests not yet answered, oldest first. The server answers in order, so the arena
+	// is a circular buffer of them: allocated at the back, freed at the front.
+	live []block
+}
+
+// Open maps the channel the server created at path. Responses left by an earlier client are discarded.
+func Open(path string) (*Client, error) {
+	file, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_RDWR, 0)
+	if err != nil {
+		return nil, err
+	}
+	defer file.Close()
+	info, err := file.Stat()
+	if err != nil {
+		return nil, err
+	}
+	total := uint64(info.Size())
+	if total < headerSize {
+		return nil, errHeader
+	}
+	data, err := syscall.Mmap(int(file.Fd()), 0, int(total), syscall.PROT_READ|syscall.PROT_WRITE, syscall.MAP_SHARED|mapPopulate)
+	if err != nil {
+		return nil, err
+	}
+	c := &Client{data: data}
+	field := func(at uint64) uint64 { return atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(at)) }
+	c.ringCap, c.reqRing, c.respRing = field(hRingCap), field(hReqRing), field(hRespRing)
+	c.arenaOff, c.arenaLen = field(hArenaOff), field(hArenaLen)
+	// Every later access is in bounds given these: the rings sit below the arena, the arena inside the file.
+	ringFits := func(ring uint64) bool {
+		return ring%8 == 0 && ring+rSlots <= c.arenaOff && c.ringCap <= (c.arenaOff-ring-rSlots)/msgSize
+	}
+	ok := field(hMagic) == magic && field(hVersion) == version && field(hTotal) == total &&
+		c.ringCap != 0 && c.ringCap&(c.ringCap-1) == 0 &&
+		c.arenaOff <= total && c.arenaLen == total-c.arenaOff &&
+		ringFits(c.reqRing) && ringFits(c.respRing)
+	if !ok {
+		syscall.Munmap(data)
+		return nil, errHeader
+	}
+	atomic.StoreUint64(c.word(c.respRing+rHead), atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(c.respRing+rTail)))
+	return c, nil
+}
+
+// Close unmaps the channel. The Client must not be used afterwards.
+func (c *Client) Close() error {
+	data := c.data
+	c.data = nil
+	return syscall.Munmap(data)
+}
+
+// word is the u64 at an 8-aligned offset; the mapping is page-aligned.
+func (c *Client) word(at uint64) *uint64 {
+	return (*uint64)(unsafe.Pointer(&c.data[at : at+8][0]))
+}
+
+func (c *Client) slot(ring, index uint64) []byte {
+	at := ring + rSlots + (index&(c.ringCap-1))*msgSize
+	return c.data[at : at+msgSize]
+}
+
+// Epoch is incremented each time the server starts. A request in flight across a restart gets no response.
+func (c *Client) Epoch() uint64 { return atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(hEpoch)) }
+
+func (c *Client) PubKeySize() int { return int(atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(hPubKeySize))) }
+func (c *Client) MessageLen() int { return int(atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(hMessageLen))) }
+func (c *Client) SigSize() int    { return int(atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(hSigSize))) }
+
+// place says where a block of n bytes goes, from the arena's start, given the blocks still held.
+func place(live []block, arenaLen, n uint64) (uint64, bool) {
+	if len(live) == 0 {
+		return 0, n <= arenaLen
+	}
+	first, last := live[0], live[len(live)-1]
+	end := last.end()
+	switch {
+	case last.off < first.off:
+		// Wrapped: the gap up to the oldest block.
+		return end, n <= first.off-end
+	case n <= arenaLen-end:
+		return end, true
+	default:
+		// Wrap into the space before the oldest block. first.off > 0 keeps last.off < first.off meaning wrapped.
+		return 0, first.off > 0 && n <= first.off
+	}
+}
+
+// Send queues a request and returns its id. respCap bytes of arena are reserved for the response:
+// a proof that does not fit is discarded by the server (StRespTooSmall).
+func (c *Client) Send(op, flags, logInvRate uint32, payload []byte, respCap int) (uint64, error) {
+	tail := atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(c.reqRing + rTail))
+	if tail-atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(c.reqRing+rHead)) >= c.ringCap {
+		return 0, ErrFull
+	}
+	if respCap < 0 || uint64(respCap) > c.arenaLen || uint64(len(payload)) > c.arenaLen {
+		return 0, ErrFull
+	}
+	b := block{payloadLen: uint64(len(payload)), respCap: uint64(respCap)}
+	off, ok := place(c.live, c.arenaLen, b.payloadLen+b.respCap)
+	if !ok {
+		return 0, ErrFull
+	}
+	c.nextID++
+	b.id, b.off = c.nextID, off
+	reqOff := c.arenaOff + off
+	copy(c.data[reqOff:reqOff+b.payloadLen], payload)
+
+	msg := c.slot(c.reqRing, tail)
+	le := binary.LittleEndian
+	le.PutUint64(msg[0:], b.id)
+	le.PutUint32(msg[8:], op)
+	le.PutUint32(msg[12:], flags)
+	le.PutUint64(msg[16:], reqOff)
+	le.PutUint64(msg[24:], b.payloadLen)
+	le.PutUint64(msg[32:], reqOff+b.payloadLen)
+	le.PutUint64(msg[40:], b.respCap)
+	le.PutUint32(msg[48:], logInvRate)
+	clear(msg[52:])
+	atomic.StoreUint64(c.word(c.reqRing+rTail), tail+1)
+	c.live = append(c.live, b)
+	return b.id, nil
+}
+
+// TryRecv returns the next response, if the server has produced one. It frees the request's arena
+// block, and those of earlier requests that a server restart left unanswered.
+func (c *Client) TryRecv() (Response, bool) {
+	head := atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(c.respRing + rHead))
+	if atomic.LoadUint64(c.word(c.respRing+rTail)) == head {
+		return Response{}, false
+	}
+	msg := c.slot(c.respRing, head)
+	le := binary.LittleEndian
+	r := Response{ID: le.Uint64(msg[0:]), Status: le.Uint32(msg[8:]), Detail: le.Uint32(msg[12:]), RespLen: le.Uint64(msg[16:])}
+	atomic.StoreUint64(c.word(c.respRing+rHead), head+1)
+
+	for len(c.live) > 0 && c.live[0].id < r.ID {
+		c.live = c.live[1:]
+	}
+	if len(c.live) > 0 && c.live[0].id == r.ID {
+		b := c.live[0]
+		c.live = c.live[1:]
+		if r.Status != StRespTooSmall && r.RespLen <= b.respCap {
+			respOff := c.arenaOff + b.off + b.payloadLen
+			r.Body = append([]byte(nil), c.data[respOff:respOff+r.RespLen]...)
+		}
+	}
+	return r, true
+}
diff --git a/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/client_test.go b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/client_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..67cc2d8fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/client_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+package leanvmsidecar
+
+import "testing"
+
+// Random sends and in-order frees: a placed block is inside the arena and overlaps no live one.
+func TestBlocksNeverOverlap(t *testing.T) {
+	const arenaLen = 100
+	var live []block
+	state, placed := uint64(1), 0
+	for id := uint64(0); id < 10000; id++ {
+		state = state*6364136223846793005 + 1442695040888963407
+		n := (state >> 33) % 40
+		if off, ok := place(live, arenaLen, n); ok {
+			if off+n > arenaLen {
+				t.Fatalf("block [%d, %d) outside the arena", off, off+n)
+			}
+			for _, b := range live {
+				if off+n > b.off && b.end() > off {
+					t.Fatalf("block [%d, %d) overlaps [%d, %d)", off, off+n, b.off, b.end())
+				}
+			}
+			live = append(live, block{id: id, off: off, payloadLen: n})
+			placed++
+		} else {
+			live = live[1:]
+		}
+		if state>>63 == 1 && len(live) > 0 {
+			live = live[1:]
+		}
+	}
+	if placed <= 1000 {
+		t.Fatal("too few blocks placed")
+	}
+}
diff --git a/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/e2e/main.go b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/e2e/main.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..85edc2b5b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go/e2e/main.go
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+// The run e2e.sh drives: e2e <channel> <signatures-file> <aggregate-rate> <recurse-rate>
+//
+// Sixteen AGGREGATE requests of 1500 signatures each, one after the other, then one RECURSE over
+// the sixteen proofs. The file is records of pubkey | message | signature.
+package main
+
+import (
+	"encoding/binary"
+	"fmt"
+	"os"
+	"strconv"
+	"time"
+
+	leanvmsidecar "github.com/leanEthereum/leanVM/bins/leanvm-sidecar/clients/go"
+)
+
+const (
+	batches  = 16
+	perBatch = 1500
+	respCap  = 16 << 20
+)
+
+func fatal(err error) {
+	if err != nil {
+		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, err)
+		os.Exit(1)
+	}
+}
+
+// call sends one request and waits for its response.
+func call(client *leanvmsidecar.Client, op, flags, rate uint32, payload []byte) (leanvmsidecar.Response, time.Duration) {
+	started := time.Now()
+	id, err := client.Send(op, flags, rate, payload, respCap)
+	fatal(err)
+	for {
+		response, ok := client.TryRecv()
+		if !ok {
+			time.Sleep(100 * time.Microsecond)
+			continue
+		}
+		if response.ID != id {
+			fatal(fmt.Errorf("response %d to request %d", response.ID, id))
+		}
+		return response, time.Since(started)
+	}
+}
+
+// split cuts a proof | claims body into the two, each with its length prefix.
+func split(response leanvmsidecar.Response) (proof, claims []byte) {
+	if response.Status != leanvmsidecar.StOK {
+		fmt.Printf("  FAILED: status %d detail %d: %s\n", response.Status, response.Detail, response.Body)
+		os.Exit(1)
+	}
+	proofLen := binary.LittleEndian.Uint64(response.Body)
+	return response.Body[:8+proofLen], response.Body[8+proofLen:]
+}
+
+func main() {
+	if len(os.Args) != 5 {
+		fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, "usage: e2e <channel> <signatures-file> <aggregate-rate> <recurse-rate>")
+		os.Exit(2)
+	}
+	aggregateRate, err := strconv.ParseUint(os.Args[3], 10, 32)
+	fatal(err)
+	recurseRate, err := strconv.ParseUint(os.Args[4], 10, 32)
+	fatal(err)
+	client, err := leanvmsidecar.Open(os.Args[1])
+	fatal(err)
+	defer client.Close()
+	record := client.PubKeySize() + client.MessageLen() + client.SigSize()
+	signatures, err := os.ReadFile(os.Args[2])
+	fatal(err)
+	if len(signatures) < batches*perBatch*record {
+		fatal(fmt.Errorf("signature file too short"))
+	}
+
+	total := time.Now()
+	le := binary.LittleEndian
+	recurse := le.AppendUint32(nil, batches)
+	for batch := 0; batch < batches; batch++ {
+		payload := le.AppendUint32(nil, perBatch)
+		payload = append(payload, signatures[batch*perBatch*record:(batch+1)*perBatch*record]...)
+		response, elapsed := call(client, leanvmsidecar.OpAggregate, 0, uint32(aggregateRate), payload)
+		proof, claims := split(response)
+		fmt.Printf("aggregate %2d/%d: %d signatures, %d bytes, rate %d -> proof %d bytes, %d claims, %.3f s\n",
+			batch+1, batches, perBatch, len(payload), aggregateRate, len(proof)-8, le.Uint32(claims), elapsed.Seconds())
+		recurse = append(recurse, claims...)
+		recurse = append(recurse, proof...)
+	}
+	response, elapsed := call(client, leanvmsidecar.OpRecurse, 0, uint32(recurseRate), recurse)
+	proof, claims := split(response)
+	fmt.Printf("recurse %d -> 1: %d proofs, %d bytes, rate %d -> proof %d bytes, %d claims, %.3f s\n",
+		batches, batches, len(recurse), recurseRate, len(proof)-8, le.Uint32(claims), elapsed.Seconds())
+	fmt.Printf("total: %.3f s\n", time.Since(total).Seconds())
+}
